    "classification": "non_eea_to_eea",
    "description": "Post-Brexit, British nationals are third-country nationals for French immigration (transition period ended 1 January 2021). The standard route for salaried employment is a long-stay visa serving as a residence permit (VLS-TS) under the Salarié or Passeport-Talent scheme, followed by an online ANEF validation within 3 months of arrival. British nationals retain Schengen short-stay exemption (90 days / 180-day period) for tourism/business, but any stay >90 days or with paid work requires a long-stay visa."
  },
